---
import InfoLayout from "@/layouts/InfoLayout.astro";

export const prerender = true;
---

<InfoLayout
  heading="Terms of use"
  description="Terms for using Quick Pantry to manage recipes, meals, and grocery lists."
>
  <p>
    Quick Pantry, maintained by James Quick, helps you manage recipes, plan
    meals, and build grocery lists. These terms apply when you use the service
    or connect an AI client to it.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="account-use">
    <h2 id="account-use">Your account and connections</h2>
    <p>
      Use an account you control and keep your sign-in details and MCP keys
      private. Authorize an AI client only if you want it to access your account
      through the permissions you approve. Review requested changes carefully;
      replacing a weekly meal plan replaces that whole week's entries.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="your-content">
    <h2 id="your-content">Recipes and imported content</h2>
    <p>
      You are responsible for the content you save or import and for having
      permission to use it. Review imported or AI-generated recipes before
      cooking, including ingredient amounts, instructions, and any allergy or
      dietary requirements. Grocery costs are estimates.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="acceptable-use">
    <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not access another person's account or private data, bypass access
      controls or rate limits, or disrupt the service. Use integrations only
      with an account you are authorized to connect.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="availability">
    <h2 id="availability">Availability and questions</h2>
    <p>
      Live recipes, meal plans, orders, and edits require a network connection.
      Imports and search can fail or be unavailable, and photo import may not
      be enabled for every account.
    </p>
    <p>
      See <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> for data handling or
      <a href="/support">Support</a> for questions and problems.
    </p>
  </section>
</InfoLayout>
